('# Deploying Streamlit to GCP Cloud Run with Terraform

Based on the context provided, here's the complete serverless container approach:

## Prerequisites

```bash
gcloud auth application-default login
```

## Step 1: Build & Push Docker Image

```bash
gcloud builds submit --tag us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/<PROJECT>/<your-app>/app:latest .
```

**Ensure your `Dockerfile` includes:**
- Base image with Python
- `streamlit` in requirements (or pip install)
- Entry point: `CMD ["streamlit", "run", "app.py", "--server.port=8080"]`

## Step 2: Create Terraform Configuration

**`terraform/main.tf`:**

```hcl
provider "google" {
  project = var.gcp_project
  region  = var.gcp_region
}

resource "google_cloud_run_service" "app" {
  name     = var.service_name
  location = var.gcp_region

  template {
    spec {
      containers {
        image = "us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/${var.gcp_project}/${var.registry_name}/app:latest"

        ports {
          container_port = 8080
        }

        # Optional: Set memory/CPU
        resources {
          limits = {
            memory = "512Mi"
            cpu    = "1"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  traffic {
    percent         = 100
    latest_revision = true
  }

  depends_on = [google_artifact_registry_repository.repo]
}

# Make service publicly accessible
resource "google_cloud_run_service_iam_member" "public" {
  service       = google_cloud_run_service.app.name
  location      = google_cloud_run_service.app.location
  role          = "roles/run.invoker"
  member        = "allUsers"
}

resource "google_artifact_registry_repository" "repo" {
  repository_id = var.registry_name
  format        = "DOCKER"
  location      = var.gcp_region
}

output "cloud_run_service_url" {
  value       = google_cloud_run_service.app.status[0].url
  description = "The URL of the deployed Cloud Run service"
}
```

**`terraform/variables.tf`:**

```hcl
variable "gcp_project" {
  type = string
}

variable "gcp_region" {
  type    = string
  default = "us-central1"
}

variable "service_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "streamlit-app"
}

variable "registry_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "streamlit-registry"
}
```

**`terraform/terraform.tfvars`:**

```hcl
gcp_project = "your-project-id"
gcp_region  = "us-central1"
service_name = "streamlit-app"
registry_name = "streamlit-registry"
```

## Step 3: Deploy

```bash
cd terraform
terraform init
terraform apply
```

## Step 4: Get Your Public URL

```bash
terraform output cloud_run_service_url
```

Output format: `https://<service>-<hash>-uc.a.run.app`

## Key Points

- **Streamlit port:** Must be `8080` (Cloud Run requirement)
- **Public access:** `google_cloud_run_service_iam_member` makes it reviewable
- **Cold starts:** First request may take 5-10 seconds
- **Database access:** If using Postgres/Grafana, ensure Cloud Run has network access (VPC Connector if needed)

This gives you the **+2 Cloud Deployment bonus** with a shareable URL for peer review.', Usage(cache_creation=CacheCreation(ephemeral_1h_input_tokens=0, ephemeral_5m_input_tokens=0), cache_creation_input_tokens=0, cache_read_input_tokens=0, inference_geo='not_available', input_tokens=906, output_tokens=941, output_tokens_details=None, server_tool_use=None, service_tier='standard', speed='standard'))
